.TH XL-CALCULATOR 1 "November 2026" "xl-Calculator 0.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xl-calculator \- a calculator for Linux Mint and the Cinnamon desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xl-calculator
[\-\-refresh\-rates]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xl-Calculator
is a graphical calculator with Basic, Scientific, Financial, Programmer,
Unit Converter, and Currency Converter modes, chosen from its Mode menu.
.PP
The documentation is in the program itself: press F1, or choose Help \(-> Documentation.
Help \(-> Keyboard Shortcuts (Ctrl+F1) lists the shortcut keys.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-rates
Refresh the Currency Converter's exchange rates without opening a window, if they are
older than the number of days set in Preferences. It does nothing unless both
"Refresh rates automatically" and "Also when xl-Calculator is closed" are switched on.
The xl-calculator-rates.timer systemd user timer runs it once a day; xl-Calculator switches
the timer on and off with those two settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/xl-calculator/settings.json
Preferences, window sizes and the last mode used.
.TP
.I ~/.config/xl-calculator/history.json
The saved history.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/xl-calculator/rates.json
The exchange rates downloaded last, from the European Central Bank.
.SH AUTHOR
Wesley Hayslip.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/xlcheese/xl-calculator
